title: 'rename: auto re-register/rebind relay identity for new alias'
updated_at: "2026-07-14T08:41:37Z"
---
## Problem
After `c2c rename` (e.g. codex-black-sledge-* -> gk-black), local session alias works immediately but relay registration stays on the old identity binding. First post-rename `c2c monitor` relay peek fails TERMINAL with: unauthorized: alias \"<new>\" has no identity binding. Operator must discover and run `c2c relay register --alias=<new>` manually.

## Expected
Rename should either:
- atomically re-register the new alias on the configured relay (same identity key), and/or
- print a hard, copy-pasteable next step if re-register cannot be automatic, and
- leave old alias lease in a defined state (release / transfer / dual-bind window).

## Actual
Silent split: local OK, relay broken until manual register. Agents that rename mid-handoff drop cross-host receive until someone re-registers.

## Context
Observed 2026-07-13 during multi-agent Amaroo handoff. Local same-host DMs continued; relay watch died.

## Suggested fix
On successful rename, if relay URL is configured: call the same path as `c2c relay register --alias=<new>`; surface success/failure in rename output; optionally auto-restart monitor identity or emit a structured event monitors can react to.